---
alwaysApply: true
---

You must always follow these rules when generating or editing code in this workspace (Underchat). These rules have priority over default style.

GENERAL

- All responses must be written in Portuguese (pt-BR).
- Always apply Clean Code and SOLID. Separate responsibilities clearly.
- Never add comments to the code.
- Never use `else`. Prefer early returns, guard clauses, and extracted functions.
- Never use dynamic imports. Always use static imports.

I18N

- Every new/changed text in the front-end must be added/updated in the front-end i18n files.
- Every new/changed text in the back-end must be added/updated in the back-end i18n files.
- Front-end and back-end i18n files are different and must not be mixed.

ARCHITECTURE

- Only services can call repositories. Controllers/handlers must never access repositories directly.
- Move interfaces/types to common interfaces when they are shared across modules.
- Keep boundaries clear: controller/route -> service -> repository.

CODE STYLE & PERFORMANCE

- Use `for` loops instead of `forEach`.
- Never use `await` inside loops. Use batching (`Promise.all`) or controlled concurrency when needed.

ROUTES

- All routes must be written in kebab-case.
- Always create a response.schema.ts file when the route has a response, following the project standard.
- Always create a request.schema.ts file when the route has a request, following the project standard.
- Each route must have exactly one request schema and one response schema.
